      "summary": "The narrator steps back and gives the empire in a page. David subdues the Philistines and takes Metheg-ammah, the bridle of the mother city, out of their hand. He smites Moab and measures the prisoners with a line — two lines to die, one full line to live — and Moab brings tribute. Northward he breaks Hadadezer son of Rehob, king of Zobah, at the Euphrates watershed, houghs the chariot horses, and when Damascus marches to the rescue he garrisons Syria itself; Toi of Hamath, Hadadezer's enemy, sends his son with vessels of silver and gold and brass, all of which David dedicates to the LORD along with the spoil of every conquered nation. In the valley of salt Edom falls, and garrisons go through all Edom. Twice the refrain sounds: 'the LORD preserved David whithersoever he went.' Then the chapter turns from the map to the ministry: Joab over the host, Jehoshaphat the recorder, Zadok and Ahimelech the priests, Seraiah the scribe, Benaiah over the Cherethites and Pelethites, and David's sons chief about the king — for David reigned over all Israel, and executed judgment and justice unto all his people.",
