      "summary": "The LORD sends Nathan to the king with a story: a rich man with exceeding many flocks, a poor man with one little ewe lamb that ate of his meat and drank of his cup and was to him as a daughter — and a traveller, for whom the rich man spared his own flock and took the poor man's lamb. David's anger blazes; the man shall restore fourfold and deserves to die. Nathan answers, 'Thou art the man,' and unrolls the sentence: the sword shall never depart from David's house, and what he did secretly shall be done against him before all Israel. David's confession is three words in Hebrew — 'I have sinned against the LORD' — and forgiveness is immediate, but not consequence: the child born to Bathsheba sickens. David fasts and lies all night upon the earth seven days; when the child dies, he rises, washes, worships, and eats, to his servants' bewilderment — 'can I bring him back again? I shall go to him, but he shall not return to me.' He comforts Bathsheba, and she bears Solomon, whom the LORD loves; Nathan names him Jedidiah, 'beloved of the LORD.' Meanwhile Joab takes Rabbah's water city and summons David to finish the siege, and the crown of the Ammonite king is set on David's head.",
